ame><surname>Elzer</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kovach</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>GT</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>In vivo and in vitro stability of the broad-host-range cloning vector pBBR1MCS in six Brucella species.</article-title><source>Plasmid</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7753908</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005368-Elzer2"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elzer</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kovach</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Roop</surname><given-names>RM</given-names><suffix>2nd</suffix></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Characterization and genetic complementation of a Brucella abortus high-temperature-requirement A (htrA) deletion mutant.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>4135</fpage><lpage>4139</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7927667</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005368-Kohler1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kohler</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekaza</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Paquet</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Walravens</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Teyssier</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Induction of dnaK through its n