cellular growth of Brucella suis within U937-derived phagocytes.</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>701</fpage><lpage>712</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8793869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005368-Laskowska1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laskowska</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuczynska-Wisnik</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Skorko-Glonek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Degradation by proteases Lon, Clp and HtrA, of Escherichia coli proteins aggregated in vivo by heat shock; HtrA protease action in vivo and in vitro.</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>555</fpage><lpage>571</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8939438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005368-Lipinska1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lipinska</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Zylicz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Georgopoulos</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>The HtrA (DegP) protein, essential for Escherichia coli survival at high temperatures, is an endopeptidase.</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><volume>172</volume><fpage>1791</fpage><lpage>1797</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2180903</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005368-Strauch1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Strauch</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Beckwith</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><article-title>An Escherichia coli mutation preventing degradation of